==Syndication==
===United States===
After its primary run in broadcast syndication, the series aired on [[A&E Network]] for many years.  It then aired on [[TV Land]] from 2005 to 2008, then began airing on Encore Classic on December 2, 2013. From 2016 to 2022, the show aired on [[Laff (TV network)|Laff]].<ref>[https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/night-court-is-back-in-session-laff---the-nations-first-comedy-driven-broadcast-television-network---to-add-popular-series-on-jan-4-2016-300197878.html Night Court is Back in Session: LAFF - The Nation's First Comedy-Driven Broadcast Television Network - To Add Popular Series on Jan 4, 2016 - PR Newswire.com]</ref>

As of September 2025, the series airs on the [[Weigel Broadcasting]] owned [[Decades (TV network)|Catchy Comedy]] network on Saturdays.<ref>[https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/decades-network-catchy-comedy-night-court-1235521267/ Weigel Broadcasting‘s Decades Network Will Flip to Sitcom-Centric ‘Catchy Comedy’ in March, Led by Original ‘Night Court’ - Variety.com]</ref><ref>{{cite web | title=Watch Night Court on Catchy Comedy | url=https://www.catchycomedy.com/shows/night-court }}</ref>  The series was also the subject of Catchy Comedy's inaugural weekend "Catchy Binge" on April 1–2, 2023. Since June 2024, it is now also broadcast on [[IFC (American TV channel)|IFC]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=TV Schedule Lineup {{!}} Listing of Shows & Movies for Today {{!}} IFC |url=https://www.ifc.com/schedule/ |access-date=June 13, 2024 |website=www.ifc.com |language=en}}</ref> usually airing in marathons on Mondays and Tuesdays, and sometimes an episode or two is shown in the early mornings on weekends.

===Australia===
[[Network Ten]] first broadcast the series in the 1980s and 1990s. [[7TWO]] began showing reruns in June 2011. Reruns are currently being shown on [[Foxtel]] Comedy Channel. {{Citation needed|date=January 2023}}

===Canada===
Aired weekdays on both [[Comedy Gold (TV channel)|Comedy Gold]] and JoyTV.{{Citation needed|date=January 2023}}

===Germany===
[[Sat.1]] aired the series as ''[[:de:Harrys wundersames Strafgericht|Harry's wundersames Strafgericht]]'' (''Harry's Miraculous Criminal Court'') in 1988.{{Citation needed|date=January 2023|reason=Possible circular reference via wikilink?}}

===Italy===
[[Italia 1]] aired the show as ''[[:it:Giudice di notte|Giudice di notte]]'' (''Night Judge'') from 1986 until 1988.{{Citation needed|date=January 2023|reason=Possible circular reference via wikilink?}}

===Spain===
TVE aired the show as ''Juzgado de Guardia'' (''Court on Duty/Call'').{{Citation needed|date=January 2023}}

===New Zealand===
The show screened weekly on [[TVNZ 1]] in the 1980s and 1990s, and was rerun in the late 1990s.{{Citation needed|date=January 2023}}

==Home media==
[[Warner Home Video]] released the first three seasons on DVD in [[DVD region code|Region]] 1.  Seasons 4–9 were released as Manufacture-on-Demand (MOD) DVDs as part of the [[Warner Archive Collection]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tvshowsondvd.com/news/Night-Court-Season-9/18565|title=Night Court DVD news: Announcement for Night Court – The Complete 9th Season|website=TVShowsOnDVD.com|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130613024212/http://tvshowsondvd.com/news/Night-Court-Season-9/18565|archive-date=June 13, 2013|df=mdy-all}}</ref>

On June 13, 2023, Warner Bros. (through Studio Distribution Services) released ''Night Court: The Complete Series'' on DVD in Region 1.<ref name="Amazon2023">[https://www.amazon.com/Night-Court-Complete-Harry-Anderson/dp/B0C3HZ67YD Night Court: The Complete Series]</ref>

